<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Cockerill unions to strike on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Belgian Cockerill unions to strike on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unions at Belgian steel producer Cockerill Sambre plan a general 24-hour strike on October 22, they said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The strike is in protest of a restructuring plan at the group, which last month published a 180 million franc loss for the first half of 1996, reversing a 3.1 billion franc profit in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>The unions -- CNE and SETCA -- said they were opposed to all possible future job cuts. They also want a 32-hour work week without loss of pay.</p>
